  "version": 194,
  "released": "2026-08-22",
  "changelog": "v194: chronology research \u2014 historians' method, life-history calendars, and the psychology of dating memories. Docs/research only, nothing implemented. NEW system/research/chronology.md: a sourced literature review of how historians and biographers build chronologies (terminus post/ante quem bounding, conjectural-date convention from documentary editing, Hermione Lee's craft testimony that a chronological spine underlies thematic structure), oral-history method and the life history calendar (Freedman et al. 1988, Belli 1998's sequential/parallel retrieval cueing), the psychology of dating autobiographical memories (Friedman 1993, Brown/Rips/Shevell 1985, telescoping and rounding per Loftus & Marburger 1983 and Huttenlocher/Hedges/Bradburn 1990, Conway & Pleydell-Pearce 2000's lifetime-period hierarchy, the living-in-history effect), how historians and oral historians (Portelli) treat disagreement as data rather than a defect to resolve, chronology as the empirical substrate of narrative identity (McAdams & McLean 2013), and an eleven-step elicitation playbook for an AI placing memories on a timeline \u2014 the seed for a future `timeline` child interaction, noted in interactions/README.md's new 'Proposed, not built' list (no interaction files yet). NEW system/research/QUEUE.md: the 12-item research backlog in priority order, as the repo's first research-ingestion queue. CORPUS CORRECTION in system/research.md: the long-standing 'Dating memories' bullet under \u00a74 cited landmark anchoring raising correct dating '~42%\u219268%' to an unlocatable 'Zwartz 2013' \u2014 replaced with the sourced claim (Glasner & van der Vaart 2009; van der Vaart & Glasner 2011: landmark components alone give only weak positive effects, whole life-history-calendar instruments give the large gains), design implication unchanged (never open with 'what year'). \u00a72a's 'unchanged from v1' hybrid thematic-chronological claim is now sourced to Lee's Paris Review interview. \u00a79 Key References: the stray Zwartz 2013 citation replaced with the correct sources, plus a new 'Chronology & historical method' reference line. NEW \u00a74a in research.md summarizes all six findings in the existing voice, citing the full file and the queue. Contract: none (research-only, per owner direction 2026-08-22).",
